    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nI use `vim-sexp` for lisps, which has its own pairing implementation, so `mini.pairs`'s isn't needed. They coexist just fine, but I don't want the `'` rule when writing lisp.\r\n\r\nAdding an option to specify the file types to exclude would be great.",
