    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You can disable any module of 'mini.nvim' per buffer by setting buffer local variable of the format `vim.b.minixxx_disable` to `true`. This will be [`vim.b.minipairs_disable = true` for 'mini.pairs'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L73).\r\n\r\nThere is a section in help for [most common disabling recipes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini.txt#L250). In your case it would be \"Disable for a certain filetype\", so it should be solved by creating autocommand for appropriate filetypes.",
